ange for maturing securities) tenders accepted on behalf of foreign/international monetary authorities (global non-domestic investors).\n\n\nI'll compute the precise values: $10,102 million represents the total investor bids, with $478 million being noncash rollover tenders from foreign investors. This translates to 4.73% of the total bids, confirming my earlier calculation.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_69e7076c48d94661a3025ba2","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"todo__todo_write","arguments":{"content":"- [x] Read the Treasury Bulletin page 13 text to find the 2-year note auction details\n- [ ] Identify total dollar value of bids submitted for 2-year Treasury notes maturing July 1984\n- [ ] Identify noncash rollover tenders accepted for foreign/international authorities\n- [ ] Calculate percentage of noncash rollover tenders\n- [ ] Write final answer to /app/answer.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"todo"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
